                <pb facs="0663" n="569" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg569"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Embassy of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-01-25"><hi rendition="#italic">January 25,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Informed by foreign office Her Majesty’s high commission, South Africa,
                    telegraphs colonial secretary American citizens arrested in Transvaal are all
                    well and in good spirits; all out on bail, on parole to remain in Pretoria,
                    excepting Hammond, who is still imprisoned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
